{
  "requirement": "The `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents adding, changing, or removing end-user-observable behavior that no agreed requirement already specifies in a Habeas project to draft requirements and commit them, once agreed under {cite}`requirements.cli.requirements_review_skill.agreement` and {cite}`requirements.cli.requirements_review_skill.commit`, before writing implementation or test code.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "Both marked tests check the subject. They read the real `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md`, and the helpers `step_of`, `workflow_steps`, `assert_phrases` and `collapse` assert on its collapsed text.\n\nObligations derived from `requirements.cli.requirements_review_skill`:\n\n1. **Scope.** The skill must direct agents adding, changing or removing end-user-observable behavior that no agreed requirement specifies.\n   - `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_reviews_every_change_to_agreed_text]` asserts that the workflow contains the exemption wording. That wording is \"If the change adds, alters, or removes no observable behavior\" and \"an existing requirement already specifies it (most bug fixes), tell the user which requirement covers it\".\n   - The same test asserts that the description contains \"before changing code, tests, or requirement text\".\n   - The same test asserts that every change to agreed text, including a rewording or a removal, goes through steps 3 to 5.\n   - `the_requirements_skill_commits_agreed_requirements_before_code` asserts that every end-user-observable result, including errors and input handling, must follow from an agreed requirement.\n2. **Draft requirements.** `the_requirements_skill_commits_agreed_requirements_before_code` locates the \"Write drafts\" step. It asserts that this step comes before review, the gate, the commit and implementation.\n3. **Commit once agreed, before implementation or test code.** The same test locates five steps:\n   - the draft step;\n   - the review step (\"start a read-only subagent\");\n   - the exact gate sentence (\"no implementation or test code, and no commit, until the user has agreed to, rejected, or deferred every group\");\n   - the commit step (\"then commit it, all groups together, before any code\");\n   - the \"Implement and test\" step.\n\n   It then asserts `draft < review && review < gate && gate < commit && commit < implement`. A skill that let code, tests or the commit come before agreement would fail this ordering. A skill that dropped the gate or the commit wording would fail the lookups.\n\nI read the skill's workflow steps 1 to 7 and the trailing paragraph. They contain each asserted phrase, and the step order matches the test's expectations: draft is step 2, review 3, the gate 4, commit 5, implement 6.\n\nThe cited `.agreement` and `.commit` requirements are context. Their gate and \"all groups together\" wording is also exercised here. The \"leaving out uncommitted edits\" detail belongs to the cited `.commit` requirement, so I did not assess it here.\n\nI found no requirement-violating skill text that these tests would accept. The tests do not assert that the exemption routes to step 6. The subject does not require that routing, so I did not count it as a gap.",
  "references": "92bfb2508d227958b775e037320a82501c0b733b2fca5be678d89f5d5579945f",
  "inputs": [
